{"_comment":"P3-D: the contract-3 open-water layer (cells.json tile_water / tile_body) of every shipped structured map, run-length encoded ([value, count] over the row-major data), for tests/deep_water_verdict_diff, which grafts it onto the shipped cells.json. Made from TG contract-3 dumps (tools/headless_dump.gd for the layout maps, windowed sandbox exports for the procedural ones) whose every other cells.json key equals the shipped file. Each map's cells_md5 is the md5 of the shipped <id>_cells.json text (CR bytes dropped) the layer was checked against: a re-exported map fails the diff until it is re-packed. A map whose shipped cells.json carries its own tile_water / tile_body (contract 3, e.g. the Perrow tg_hillside_* water maps) needs no record: the diff strips that layer for OLD and uses the shipped file as NEW, and the packer skips it. Re-pack: python tools/pack_c3_water_layers.py <dir of contract-3 <id>_cells.json> [--merge] (from the project folder); python tools/pack_c3_water_layers.py --check lists the stale maps.","maps":{"combat_test":{"layer":false,"cells_md5":"a7b9b6c58adaf59bc5517d8afdc9a876"},"tg_castle_demo":{"layer":false,"cells_md5":"e5cc1692c75898bf185927899a538b8d"},"tg_castle_keep":{"layer":false,"cells_md5":"5601d3664db4acf8cae6010804e9a528"},"tg_cemetery":{"layer":false,"cells_md5":"64316d8c0aed2d8d1dd2df599543ece2"},"tg_courthouse":{"layer":false,"cells_md5":"2a8e03e496fa0a38194eb363504b5d96"},"tg_export":{"layer":true,"cols":71,"rows":84,"tile_water":[[0.0,205],[-0.7,1],[0.0,451],[-0.7,4],[0.0,34],[-0.7,1],[0.0,23],[-0.7,11],[0.0,2],[-0.7,4],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,71],[-0.7,5],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,70],[-0.7,2],[0.0,70],[-0.7,1],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,11],[-0.7,1],[0.0,59],[-0.7,1],[0.0,70],[-0.7,1],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,142],[-0.7,3],[0.0,70],[-0.7,2],[0.0,71],[-0.7,3],[0.0,70],[-0.7,2],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,70],[-0.7,1],[0.0,72],[-0.7,1],[0.0,70],[-0.7,2],[0.0,71],[-0.7,1],[0.0,73],